# Always resolve against the public npm registry, never a corporate mirror.
#
# npm records the registry it used in `resolved` and, when a mirror strips the
# upstream sha512, downgrades `integrity` to sha1. Regenerating this lockfile on
# a machine whose global npmrc points at an internal proxy therefore rewrites all
# 86 entries to that proxy's URLs with sha1 hashes, which binds this public repo's
# CI to an internal mirror and weakens the integrity check. Pinning the registry
# here means such a machine fails loudly instead.
registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
